# These files are compared byte for byte against the payload inside fixture.msi, which was
# built from them. Line-ending normalisation would rewrite them on checkout, the digests would
# stop matching, and the tests would fail in a fresh clone while passing here — the exact
# "works on my machine" trap the committed fixture exists to avoid.
#
# -text: store and check out verbatim, whatever core.autocrlf says.
* -text
*.msi binary
